  "documents": {
   "text": "The covenant terms of the lamar_2007 indenture include the following confirmed and not confirmed values: The Company's Leverage Ratio must be less than 7.0 to 1 (Section 4.10, confirmed). For restricted payments, immediately after giving effect to such Restricted Payment, the aggregate of all Restricted Payments declared or made after the Existing Notes Issue Date does not exceed the sum of 100% of the Company's Cumulative EBITDA minus 1.4 times the Company's Cumulative Consolidated Interest Expense (Section 4.11, not confirmed). Also in Section 4.11, 100% of the aggregate Net Proceeds and the fair market value of securities or other property received by the Company after January 1, 2001, from certain specified sources is noted (not confirmed). The Asset Sale threshold is $10 million (Section 1.01, not confirmed). If on the Reinvestment Date with respect to any Asset Sale, the Available Asset Sale Proceeds exceed $25 million, the Company shall apply an amount equal to such Available Asset Sale Proceeds to an offer to repurchase the Notes (Section 4.13, confirmed). The Change of Control Purchase Price is 101% of the principal amount plus accrued and unpaid interest (Section 4.19, not confirmed). For Affiliate Transactions, amounts in excess of $5 million require a Board Resolution (Section 4.14, confirmed), and amounts in excess of $20 million require a written opinion from an independent investment banking firm (Section 4.14, confirmed).\n\nFrom Item 2.03 of the Form 8-K with accession 0001193125-25-064058, the principal amount stated is $500 million, the interest rate is 6.700%, and the maturity year is 2055.",
